PURPOSE

Explain what the frozen A45
5:3 "oscillation" actually consists of
after the one-epoch cooperative echo
substantially improves third-hit core survival.

This diagnostic replays
the frozen A45 primary worlds
with observational timeline instrumentation only.

No dynamics,
RNG,
arm,
threshold,
qualification,
or A45 conclusion is changed.

OSCILLATOR DETECTOR AUDIT

The inherited oscillator detector
examines majority labels after epoch 8.

Every majority-label transition counts.

Therefore:

favored -> unresolved -> favored

counts as two transitions,

just as:

favored -> adverse -> favored

would count as two transitions.

A world is classified oscillatory
when post-epoch-8 majority-label changes >= 4.

The detector therefore does not distinguish
harmful side-to-side capture
from temporary loss of majority into uncertainty.

